WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.840
Otherwise known as Agent 13, Sharon Carter is&nbsp;
one of S.H.I.E.L.D.'s deadliest operatives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.520
But what's the full story behind this legendary&nbsp;
ally of Captain America? From her family roots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.160
to her most dangerous missions, this&nbsp;
is the untold truth of Sharon Carter.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.880
One thing worth knowing is that Sharon&nbsp;
Carter wasn't actually the first Agent 13:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.840
Her aunt Margaret "Peggy" Carter holds that&nbsp;
distinction. During her time as Agent 13,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.680
Peggy fights in the French resistance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.760
falls in love with Captain America, and&nbsp;
takes on the first iteration of HYDRA.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.480
Naturally, Peggy is heartbroken when Cap&nbsp;
disappears. However, she quickly overcomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.079
her grief, joins a number of different spy&nbsp;
agencies, and eventually becomes an agent of&nbsp;S.H.I.E.L.D. 

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:45.120
Her older brother Harrison&nbsp;
later welcomes a daughter named Sharon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.401
and the two become very close - in fact, Sharon&nbsp;
sees Peggy as something of a personal hero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.401 --> 00:00:53.840
Having grown up dazzled by tales&nbsp;
of her aunt's wartime exploits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.320
Sharon decides to join S.H.I.E.L.D. -&nbsp;
and even adopts her aunt's old codename.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.920
But then Peggy suddenly relapses into grief&nbsp;
for Cap and is placed into an asylum. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.080
becomes so delusional, in fact, that she&nbsp;
imagines Sharon to be her kid sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.680
and Harrison to be her father. This&nbsp;
strange plot line was introduced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.480
mostly because of the increasing time lag&nbsp;
between World War II and the modern era.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.640
In the end, it turns out that Peggy is&nbsp;
being manipulated by Doctor Faustus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.840
but Cap rescues her and she snaps out of her&nbsp;
delirium. Cap finally convinces Peggy that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:30.400
can never be together… although he conveniently&nbsp;
leaves out the part about him dating Sharon.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.360
When Captain America first meets Sharon&nbsp;
Carter, she looks so much like Peggy that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.840
he actually thinks he's hallucinating. At the&nbsp;
time, Sharon is on a mission for S.H.I.E.L.D.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.640
trying to prevent Batroc the Leaper from&nbsp;
obtaining a chemical compound called Inferno&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:49.760
42. They later reunite while trying to&nbsp;
take down A.I.M. and MODOK. Soon after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:55.280
she helps Cap and Black Panther bring down Baron&nbsp;
Zemo after the notorious villain obtains a death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:01.120
ray - and these are just a small handful of Agent&nbsp;
13's adventures in the Silver Age of Comics.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.280
Sharon works frequently with Steve&nbsp;
Rogers during this era, but Cap never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:10.640
fully embraces her as a partner: Unfortunately,&nbsp;
he's always too worried about her personal safety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:16.480
to realize how lethal - and useful - she can be.&nbsp;
It doesn't help that he's also kinda obsessed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.120
with Bucky's death at this point, and can't&nbsp;
stand the thought of losing another partner.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.080
Both Captain America and Sharon Carter&nbsp;
flirt with retirement on multiple occasions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.360
always in the hope that they&nbsp;
might settle down together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.120
Cap is the first to consider this, when&nbsp;
they're reunited for the first time - heck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.760
he even makes plans to propose to her. When&nbsp;
he realizes he's about to be replaced by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.960
bunch of cosplayers, however, he realizes&nbsp;
that he can't hang up the shield just yet.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:48.480
Nonetheless, Cap tries to get Sharon to quit on&nbsp;
multiple occasions. At first, she's resistant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.320
to the idea, but she eventually agrees to take&nbsp;
an inactive role with S.H.I.E.L.D. that places&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:58.160
her firmly on the sidelines. Later, Sharon regains&nbsp;
her full-time role with S.H.I.E.L.D., as Nick Fury&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:03.840
claims her PhD in metaphysical psychology makes&nbsp;
her too valuable an agent to lose. Sharon is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:09.200
subsequently put in charge of an all-women cadre&nbsp;
of S.H.I.E.L.D. agents called the Femme Force.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.040
There is a brief time during which&nbsp;
Sharon decides she's had enough of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.720
S.H.I.E.L.D. and finally quits to be&nbsp;
with Cap. Not long after, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:22.320
Cap defeats the Secret Empire and learns that it's&nbsp;
headed by a high-ranking government official. He's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.120
so disillusioned by this revelation that he&nbsp;
quits his role as Captain America, and when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.801
Hawkeye talks Steve into becoming a new kind of&nbsp;
hero, Sharon is less than enthused by the idea.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.482
"You didn't see that coming?"

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.240
Ultimately, Cap's decision to walk&nbsp;
the hero's path puts an end to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.880
dreams of living an idyllic life with Sharon.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:46.320
Even by the standards of the Marvel Universe,&nbsp;
Doctor Faustus is a truly vile villain. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:51.520
entire modus operandi is violating people's&nbsp;
free will to make them his mind-slaves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.640
and the subtle nature of his powers make him&nbsp;
especially difficult to root out and destroy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.760
He manipulates Peggy Carter for years,&nbsp;
although he never learns anything of much use.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:07.120
Then William Burnside, the twisted Captain&nbsp;
America of the 1950s, comes under his control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:12.080
compelling him to become the leader of a&nbsp;
neo-Nazi group called the National Force.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.160
At this point, Cap and Sharon have been&nbsp;
on-again, off-again for a long time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:20.720
She's still mad at him for choosing life as&nbsp;
Captain America over her, and is busy flirting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:26.320
with her neighbor, the pacifist Dave Cox. Sharon&nbsp;
soon returns to active duty, and ends up acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:31.280
as a S.H.I.E.L.D. liaison for the New York police&nbsp;
during their investigation of the National Force.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:35.440
When she goes undercover, however, she&nbsp;
quickly comes under the influence of Faustus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.680
who makes her one of his foot soldiers.&nbsp;
During a battle against the National Force,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.320
Cap loses sight of Sharon, who is later&nbsp;
revealed to have self-immolated alongside a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:49.520
number of other National Force agents. For all&nbsp;
intents and purposes, Sharon Carter is dead.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.760
Except, of course, she isn't.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.560
"What a twist."

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:58.640
It's eventually revealed that Sharon has&nbsp;
actually been sent on a deep cover mission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:02.560
in Europe - but something went wrong&nbsp;
along the way. She got completely cut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:05.760
off from S.H.I.E.L.D. and ended up&nbsp;
behind enemy lines, and it took her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:10.800
years to make it out - with Captain America&nbsp;
convinced that she was dead the whole time.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:15.200
Now, at this point in comics canon, the&nbsp;
super-soldier serum has begun to take a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:20.880
toll on Cap's body. Just as he's about to die,&nbsp;
Sharon and her team whisk away his body and give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:25.680
him a total blood transfusion from the only other&nbsp;
person with the serum running through their veins:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.640
the Red Skull. As it turns out, the Red Skull&nbsp;
- who has been inhabiting a clone of Cap's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:36.640
body for years - arranged the rescue because he&nbsp;
needs the real Cap to retrieve the Cosmic Cube.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.960
The Cube is being held by a group of&nbsp;
fanatics from A.I.M. called the Kubekult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.920
a group Sharon has successfully infiltrated.&nbsp;
She puts the Cube in Cap's hands, knowing he'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:51.600
use its power for good, but Cap gets trapped&nbsp;
inside it - with Adolf Hitler, of all people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:56.400
Of course, he soon triumphs, escapes, and&nbsp;
defeats the Red Skull. Cap and Sharon are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:01.130
reunited, and their on-again, off-again&nbsp;
relationship is finally turned back on.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.680
After the "Civil War'' conflict between&nbsp;
Steve Rogers and Tony Stark turns deadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:11.040
Captain America decides to end the bloodshed&nbsp;
by turning himself in. On his way to his trial,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:17.360
however, he's gunned down by a mysterious sniper.&nbsp;
Shortly after the news of Cap's death goes public,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:22.960
Sinthia "Sin" Schmidt, daughter of the Red Skull,&nbsp;
corners a frantic Sharon in a hospital bathroom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:27.840
She then tells Sharon that Doctor Faustus&nbsp;
has a message for her: "Remember."

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:33.200
Sharon realizes, to her horror, that she has&nbsp;
killed Captain America. It turns out that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.600
whole mess has been part of an elaborate&nbsp;
brainwashing scheme perpetrated by the Red&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:42.480
Skull and Doctor Faustus, who installed&nbsp;
a subconscious trigger in Sharon's mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:48.160
and used her to seemingly kill Cap. Thankfully, it&nbsp;
turns out that Cap was merely displaced in time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:57.347
After Captain America returns from his&nbsp;
time-travel-pseudo-death, he and Sharon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.347 --> 00:07:02.547
become closer than ever. Subsequently, she&nbsp;
joins his Secret Avengers black ops team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.547 --> 00:07:06.947
and alongside a number of other heroes,&nbsp;
they chase the Serpent Crown to Mars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.947 --> 00:07:12.467
battle the Shadow Council, and uncover the&nbsp;
Thule Society, a secret order of Nazis.

00:07:12.467 --> 00:07:17.267
Then, when Peggy Carter finally dies of&nbsp;
old age, Sharon, Cap, and their allies come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.267 --> 00:07:21.747
together to mourn her passing. At the funeral,&nbsp;
however, a sniper starts shooting at them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.747 --> 00:07:26.227
and they quickly learn that the assailant&nbsp;
is the World War II hero Codename: Bravo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.227 --> 00:07:31.267
Bravo was lost on an extradimensional mission,&nbsp;
eventually returning and aligning himself with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.267 --> 00:07:36.387
a new version of HYDRA. Cap is subsequently&nbsp;
trapped in the extradimensional Land of Nowhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.387 --> 00:07:39.987
but Sharon, alongside Fury and the&nbsp;
Falcon, steps up to rescue him.

00:07:40.547 --> 00:07:44.627
One of the weirdest Cap stories ever&nbsp;
begins when a mysterious subway car&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.627 --> 00:07:49.587
arrives at an abandoned station in New York.&nbsp;
Cap climbs on board but Sharon doesn't,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.587 --> 00:07:54.543
as it only has room for one. Thus, Cap is&nbsp;
whisked away to the brutal Dimension Z,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.543 --> 00:07:59.827
an alien reality that has been conquered&nbsp;
by Cap's old enemy, Arnim Zola. Zola seeks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.827 --> 00:08:04.147
to remove the super-soldier serum from&nbsp;
Cap, in order to give it to his children.

00:08:04.147 --> 00:08:09.827
Cap spends the next dozen years trying to&nbsp;
survive, even raising Zola's son Ian as his own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.827 --> 00:08:14.387
He creates an alliance with a local tribe&nbsp;
of monsters opposed to Zola and eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.387 --> 00:08:18.707
leads a rebellion against the villain.&nbsp;
Sharon manages to track him down too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.707 --> 00:08:23.427
as only 30 minutes have passed on Earth.&nbsp;
Though Zola's daughter Jet Black switches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.427 --> 00:08:28.934
sides to join the heroes, Sharon is forced to&nbsp;
sacrifice herself to save Cap and the Earth.

00:08:28.934 --> 00:08:34.547
Predictably, however, Sharon isn't actually dead.&nbsp;
Having arrived in Dimension Z, Sharon takes over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.547 --> 00:08:40.147
Cap's role and raises Ian as her own. When she is&nbsp;
finally rescued from Dimension Z by the Falcon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.147 --> 00:08:44.147
she and Steve reunite. For a while, they&nbsp;
find peace and happiness together as they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.147 --> 00:08:48.340
coordinate the Avengers, but generally&nbsp;
refrain from going on field missions.

00:08:48.787 --> 00:08:53.587
Sharon has acted as director of S.H.I.E.L.D. on a&nbsp;
couple of different occasions. The first of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.587 --> 00:08:58.147
happens after she embarks on an expedition&nbsp;
into the Savage Land with Captain America.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.147 --> 00:09:03.267
As their mission comes to an end, a tender moment&nbsp;
between the two lovebirds is crashed by Nick Fury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.267 --> 00:09:07.801
who later reveals that he's decided&nbsp;
to appoint Sharon as his replacement.

00:09:07.801 --> 00:09:12.627
Years later, when Cap is replaced by the Cosmic&nbsp;
Cube-generated HYDRA Cap, it's revealed that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.627 --> 00:09:16.787
Red Skull was behind S.H.I.E.L.D.'s initiative&nbsp;
to use a partial Cosmic Cube to create the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.787 --> 00:09:21.827
super-villain town of Pleasant Hill. The Red Skull&nbsp;
knew that the experiment was doomed to failure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:27.027
however, and even allowed Baron Zemo to come in&nbsp;
and wreck it for good measure. This was former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.027 --> 00:09:32.947
S.H.I.E.L.D. director Maria Hill's project, and&nbsp;
as such, she takes the fall for it. Evil Cap then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.947 --> 00:09:37.907
pushes to have Sharon take the role of director.&nbsp;
Instead, Sharon recommends him for the job,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.907 --> 00:09:44.227
with a proviso that gives him absolute power&nbsp;
in case of emergency. It, uh, doesn't end well.

00:09:47.242 --> 00:09:49.507
"Hail Hydra"

00:09:50.627 --> 00:09:55.267
The "Secret Empire" event sees Sharon step down&nbsp;
as S.H.I.E.L.D. director because she thinks Steve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.267 --> 00:10:00.627
Rogers is the right man for the job. Unfortunately&nbsp;
for her and everyone else, a young, sentient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.627 --> 00:10:06.387
Cosmic Cube named Kobik has been brainwashed by&nbsp;
the Red Skull, rewriting reality such that Steve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.387 --> 00:10:12.467
Rogers has always been a deep-cover HYDRA agent.&nbsp;
Steve secretly organizes an alien attack on New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.467 --> 00:10:18.627
York, creating a state of emergency during which&nbsp;
he is awarded total control of all armed forces.

00:10:18.627 --> 00:10:24.307
Evil Cap is still in love with Sharon, however,&nbsp;
and gives her special treatment in his new regime.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.307 --> 00:10:29.107
He tries wining and dining her, then takes her&nbsp;
out to a "HYDRA Youth" science fair where they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.107 --> 00:10:33.507
see kids work on surveillance equipment&nbsp;
for hunting down Inhumans. When Evil Cap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.507 --> 00:10:37.987
survives an assassination attempt by Black&nbsp;
Widow and starts to doubt himself, he turns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.987 --> 00:10:43.427
to Sharon for reassurance. Instead, she almost&nbsp;
stabs him in the throat with a wooden stake.

00:10:43.427 --> 00:10:45.587
Feeling a little peeved by this turn of events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.587 --> 00:10:51.027
Cap puts Sharon in prison and has Doctor Faustus&nbsp;
brainwash her. Unbeknownst to Faustus, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.027 --> 00:10:56.707
Sharon has studied his voice and techniques&nbsp;
and is now immune to them. She poisons him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.707 --> 00:11:01.507
knocks him out, and uses Cap's passwords&nbsp;
to bring down his strike fleet - helping to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.507 --> 00:11:06.227
bring an end to HYDRA's reign and ushering&nbsp;
in the return of the real Captain America.

